<title>FRANCE: Latest details of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Latest details of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of November 5 in the July-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>On November 7, the EU additionally granted exports of 350,500 tonnes of soft wheat, 133,500 tonnes of barley, and 18,693 tonnes of rye.</p>
<p>Figures ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			     1Jul96 to 5 Nov96     1Jul95 to 5 Nov95</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  2,698	75     355    3,598	  802</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    1,972	74	 5    2,668	   10</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		236     118	 0	200	    0</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   28	33	 0	 84	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	185	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	    9		   0	 43	    0</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT    4,943	73     360    6,778	  812</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	   42		 139	 16	  520</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	    86     331	 0	 26	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   0	 41	    0</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     129     155     139	 83	  520</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	     5,072	74     499    6,861	1,332</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     1,996     212	16	940	   66</p>
<p>  Malt (4)	     1,723	90	 0    1,907	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  3,719     131	16    2,847	   66</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	   29    1450     182	  2	  996</p>
<p>  Food aid		   0		   -	 11	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL MAIZE		29     223     182	 13	  996</p>
<p>  Rye (grain)	    484	55	 3	883	    7</p>
<p>  Rye flour (5)	    0		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (5)	    0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL RYE		 484	55	 3	883	    7</p>
<p> OATS			183		   1	  0	    0</p>
<p>  Sorghum (grain)	  0		   3	  0	  133</p>
<p>  Food aid		   0		   -	  0	    -</p>
